48,east,"From previous observations, it seems that I am stuck in a maze with a horizontal wall to the north, east, and west, and a vertical wall to the south. The only clear path is through a doorway to the west, but I need to figure out how to get to it safely. I have a few options to consider: I can try to kick the horizontal wall to see if it opens up a new path, search the area to see if there are any hidden doors or passages, or try to go north or east to see if there is a different path. My high-level plan is to search the area and try to kick the horizontal walls to see if I can find a new path. If that doesn't work, I can try going north or east. If I get stuck, I can try to go back and re-examine my options. I will use the camera to try to get a better view of the map and maybe discover something I didn't notice before. I will keep searching and trying new things until I reach the stairs down.","message:
